-- title:
--   Non-bipartiteness of the s-isogeny graph on supersingular places
-- statement:
--   Let $M,s,q'$ be natural numbers with $M,s$ nonzero, $q'$ and $s$ prime, $q'\ge 5$, $s\ne q'$, and neither $q'$ nor $s$ dividing $M$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ has characteristic $q'$. Let $X$ be an `SSLevelDatum` for $q',\kappa,M,s$: this records that $j(q^M)$ and $j(q^s)$ lie in the field $\kappa(j(q),j(q^{Ms}))=$`modularFunctionFieldC`$\ \kappa\ (M\cdot s)$ (an intermediate field of the Laurent series over $\kappa$ generated by `jqModC` and its $q\mapsto q^{Ms}$ substitution), that the two degeneracy maps `levelAlphaC` (the inclusion of $\kappa(j(q),j(q^M))$) and `levelBetaC` (substitution $q\mapsto q^s$) and all the Hecke maps `heckeAlphaC`, `heckeBetaC` are integral, that restriction along these two maps sends places in `ssPlaces`$\ q'\ (M\cdot s)\ \kappa$ into `ssPlaces`$\ q'\ M\ \kappa$ (the places satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace`), an Atkin–Lehner automorphism interchanging the two standard generators and preserving the supersingular places, and modular polynomial data satisfying the Kronecker congruence. Then for every nonempty set $P$ of supersingular places at level $M$ there exists a supersingular place $W$ at level $M\cdot s$ with $X.\mathrm{fst}\,W\in P \iff X.\mathrm{snd}\,W\in P$, that is, whose two degeneracy images lie both in $P$ or both outside $P$.
--
--   In graph-theoretic terms, the $s$-isogeny multigraph on the supersingular points of $X_0(M)$ in characteristic $q'$, whose edge set is the supersingular locus at level $Ms$ with the two degeneracy maps as endpoints, admits no proper two-colouring; this is one of the arithmetic inputs of Ribet's surjectivity argument for the degeneracy map on degree-zero divisor groups. It is used in the proof of [`ModularCurve.SSLevelDatum.exists_mem_characterLattice_degeneracyMatrix_mulVec_eq_pair`](thm.html#ModularCurve.SSLevelDatum.exists_mem_characterLattice_degeneracyMatrix_mulVec_eq_pair).
